id:                     E6409
trigger_tool:           conan|pkg-config|meson|clang
phase:                  generate|cross-build
error_signature:        fatal error: 'opusfile.h' file not found|fatal error: 'ogg/ogg.h' file not found|dependency opusfile found but public provider edge missing

severity:               1
category:               conan|pkg-config|components|include-path|provider-contract
match_keywords:         PkgConfigDeps, Conan component, nested include, opusfile.h, include/opus, generated pc, cpp_info, Meson dependency found
title:                  Repair generated component pkg-config contracts and mandatory public provider edges

root_cause:             A Conan provider can expose libraries through a named component while its inherited includedirs still point only at the package root include directory. PkgConfigDeps generates that component .pc from component metadata, so mutating a temporary root cpp_info object in the consumer may not affect the generated Cflags. Meson then reports the dependency found although compilation cannot resolve the nested public header. Even when the component include/lib metadata is complete, an early no-repair return can still omit a required public pkg-config edge such as `ogg` for `opusfile.h`'s `ogg/ogg.h` include.
affected_scope:         Conan 2 consumers using PkgConfigDeps with a published component whose public header lives below a nested include directory not represented by the generated component .pc file.
verification_cmd:       Run a strict rewrite matrix and mandatory-edge positive/negative matrix, then require fresh isolated conan install --build=never with regular `ogg.pc` and exact `Requires: ogg opus`; finally require a single-launch target build with all 24 upstream entries and the installed-package flow passing.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           narrow-post-generation-provider-contract-repair
rec_description:        Validate the exact header and library in the dependency package, run PkgConfigDeps normally, then strictly parse and repair only the affected generated component .pc. Preserve Conan-generated name and version, require exact public `Requires` edges, and reject ambiguous or malformed files. Do not take the no-repair fast path when a required edge still needs enforcement.
rec_command:            PkgConfigDeps.generate(); validate and rewrite only opusfile.pc to include/opus and -lopusfile while requiring exact `Requires: ogg opus`
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-consumer-recipe

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      provider-recipe-version-fix
fallback_description:   Publish a newer provider recipe whose component includedirs already expose the nested header, then remove the consumer repair after a fresh W0 proves the corrected contract.
fallback_command:       fix provider component cpp_info in a new package version; publish; re-resolve downstream with --build=never
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          dependency-recipe

forbid_1_pattern:       dependency\.cpp_info\.includedirs\s*=|self\.dependencies\[.*\]\.cpp_info\.includedirs\s*=
forbid_1_reason:        Mutating a temporary root cpp_info object does not prove that PkgConfigDeps component output changed.
forbid_1_consequence:   Meson reports the dependency found but target compilation still lacks the nested header.
forbid_2_pattern:       extra_(cxxflags|ldflags).*opusfile|CXXFLAGS.*include/opus
forbid_2_reason:        Global compiler or linker injection broadens the repair beyond the one broken provider contract.
forbid_2_consequence:   Unrelated targets inherit hidden flags and the generated pkg-config module remains semantically incomplete.

principles:             P005,P010
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E321,E327]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

